miadi-tmux — one tmux, 3.7c, on a Miadi host

  sudo apt install miadi-tmux

Installs /usr/bin/tmux 3.7c, built from the upstream release
(https://github.com/tmux/tmux/releases/tag/3.7c), and replaces Ubuntu's tmux
package (3.2a on 22.04). Packages that depend on tmux take this one.

Why one version: a tmux client cannot attach to a server of another version.
On gaia, on 2026-10-03, a 3.2a server and a 3.7c client gave "open terminal
failed: not a terminal" for every session (jgwill/gaia#90). After installing,
a server that still runs the old version cannot be attached, and the postinst
names each user who has one. With miadi-terminal's restore enabled, a server
that tmux-server.service started moves over with
  systemctl --user restart tmux-server.service
(it saves first, then restores the sessions, and tide relaunches the agents).
A server started any other way moves over from a terminal outside tmux with
  systemctl --user start tmux-save.service
  tmux kill-server
  systemctl --user start tmux-server.service
tmux kill-server ends the agents running in that server
(jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit#114, jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit#115).

The sessions that survive a reboot come from miadi-terminal:
miadi-terminal enable restore.

Source: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit, packages/miadi/deb
Build:  prep/miadi-tmux.sh compiles the release named by Version (3.7c-1 -> 3.7c).
        jgwill/gaia linux_migration/14-tmux-install-latest.sh builds the same
        release into /usr/local on a host without the package.
